<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16172" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">errābundus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		erro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>wandering to and fro</i>, <i>wandering about</i>
			(rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic. or Caes.): odor,</span>”
				<i>floating about</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 692</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nunc errabundi domos suos pervagarentur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
					29</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 31</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naves (with dispersae), Auct. B. Afr. 2, 4:
					naves vagabantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 21, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trieris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 44, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agmen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Curt.
					8, 4, 6</span></i>
			.—<b>Poet.</b> transf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestigia bovis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 6, 58</span></i>
			.</div>
